{"nodes": [{"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_ai_operating_substrate", "label": "DECISION A1: AI as Operating Substrate, Not a Feature", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A1", "rationale": "The moat is not 'we built the website' \u2014 competitors get the same models. AI is treated as the substrate of Product Resolution, Procurement Execution and Customer Trust/Support because the defensible asset is running the lowest-HSPO, highest-STP compliant cross-border operation.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_agentic_commerce_protocol", "label": "Agentic Commerce Protocol (ACP, OpenAI/Stripe)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_universal_commerce_protocol", "label": "Universal Commerce Protocol (UCP, Google)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_universal_resolver", "label": "Universal Adapter / Two-Tier Product Resolver", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A3", "rationale": "Tier 1 is the official/structured API where available, tier 2 a vision-LLM extraction fallback. This replaces one hand-built brittle scraper per marketplace, so onboarding a new source marketplace takes days rather than sprints, and DOM changes stop breaking resolution.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_vision_llm_extraction", "label": "Vision-LLM Structured Extraction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_resolver_confidence", "label": "ResolverConfidence Scoring", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A3", "rationale": "Low-confidence weight/dimension fields route to the pricing risk buffer instead of a hard quote, so an uncertain extraction degrades margin protection rather than silently producing a wrong price.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_plan_follower_procurement", "label": "Plan-Follower + Human Confirmation Procurement Pattern", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A1, \u00a7A3, \u00a7A4", "rationale": "Switching browser agents from fully autonomous to plan-follower-with-oversight raised real-world success from ~30% to ~80%; the residual ceiling is auth friction (3DS/OTP), not model capability.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_stp", "label": "STP (Straight-Through Processing) North-Star Metric", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A3, \u00a7D5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_hspo", "label": "HSPO (Human Seconds Per Order) Metric", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_landed_cost_predictor", "label": "AI Landed-Cost / Weight Predictor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A3", "rationale": "Shipping/customs estimation before warehouse receipt is the largest margin leak, so predicting actual and volumetric weight from title, category, brand and images is the single highest-ROI AI investment; until real receipt data exists, category-level priors plus an explicit risk reserve stand in.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_exception_classifier", "label": "AI Exception Classifier / Ranked Ops Queue", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_persian_trust_layer", "label": "Persian-First Trust & Support AI Layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A3", "rationale": "Strong open-source Persian LLMs are scarce, so production quality requires fine-tuning a base model on Persian plus domain data. Trust is a conversion lever, not just a support cost \u2014 proactive milestone narration in Persian differentiates against fragmented Instagram sellers.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_deterministic_ledger_ai_matcher", "label": "Deterministic Ledger + LLM Fuzzy Reconciliation Matcher", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A3", "rationale": "Money is never an LLM decision; the LLM is confined to proposing fuzzy matches between foreign-card descriptors, procurement orders and customer orders, always confirmed by a human or a rule. Target auto-match >99%.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_three_exogenous_gates", "label": "Three Exogenous Gates (payment, customs, compliance)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A2 read of the matrix", "rationale": "AI upgrades everything inside the four walls but changes nothing about foreign-payment banking, customs/importability and legal compliance. These remain the true GO/NO-GO determinants and must not be papered over by AI optimism.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_r11_extraction_hallucination", "label": "Risk R11: AI Extraction Hallucination", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_merchant_fulfillment_platform", "label": "Business Line 2: Merchant Fulfillment Platform", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "Part B", "rationale": "Instead of only competing with Iranian micro-retailers for end consumers, sell them the infrastructure \u2014 turning competitors into distribution and funding working capital through their prepaid wallets.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_wholesaler_mode", "label": "Wholesaler Mode vs Agent Mode", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7B3 Rotation 1", "rationale": "Agent mode exposes the full landed-cost breakdown and invites disintermediation; wholesaler mode quotes one delivered-to-Iran price with the source hidden and margin embedded. New merchants default to wholesaler mode, with agent-mode transparency unlocked only at higher tiers or volume commitments.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_prepaid_wallet", "label": "Prepaid Merchant Wallet Money Model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7B3 Rotation 3", "rationale": "A merchant tops up in IRR and each order debits the balance, so there is zero credit risk and the merchant funds the working capital. Escrow-collected checkout is phase 2 and credit terms are strictly gated on an AI credit score.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_enterprise_procurement_desk", "label": "Business Line 3: Enterprise Import/Export Procurement Desk", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "Part C", "rationale": "Highest value per account but highest compliance and working-capital intensity, so it is deferred to phase 3+ and entered through the lowest-risk wedge (consolidation + tracking dashboard, or a single-category managed desk).", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_shared_core_engine", "label": "One Engine, Three Demand Surfaces", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7D1, \u00a7D4", "rationale": "B2C, merchant-B2B and enterprise import are three front-ends on one shared spine; everything hard and defensible (resolver, quote engine, FX, procurement, treasury, ledger, tracking, ops console, compliance allowlist) is built once, and the lines differ only in surface, policy and pricing. Three revenue lines amortize one build.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_moat", "label": "The Moat: Compliant Operation + Logistics Data Flywheel", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7D6", "rationale": "Defensibility is neither the AI nor the website. It is a compliant foreign-payment and treasury operation, real logistics data that tightens landed-cost estimates with every delivered order, the lowest HSPO / highest STP procurement, and trust infrastructure. AI is the lever; the operation and the data are the moat.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_sequencing_roadmap", "label": "Phase Sequencing 0.3 \u2192 5 (consumer, merchant, enterprise, agentic)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7D3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_universal_resolver", "target": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_vision_llm_extraction", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_resolver_confidence", "target": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_universal_resolver", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A3 BUILD", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_revalidate_at_checkout", "target": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_r11_extraction_hallucination", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A5 R11 mitigation", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_r11_extraction_hallucination", "target": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_vision_llm_extraction", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "feasibility-revalidation-v0.2.md", "source_location": "\u00a7A5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_plan_follower_procurement", "target": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_stp", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "c